ational attention. Virginia has tilted Democratic in recent statewide contests, and Warner enters with the advantages of a well-known incumbent: roughly $16 million in cash on hand against a challenger who has raised under half a million dollars. Every major race rating, from the Cook Political Report to Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the contest in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and betting markets put Warner's chances near 98 percent.\n\nThe limited public polling, conducted in May and June, showed Warner leading by 18 to 26 points, though the pollsters are little-known. Campaign coverage has centered on data centers, affordability, and flooding, with several debates canceled or in doubt. Mizusawa, a retired general making a first statewide run, has shown neither the resources nor polling evidence to threaten the incumbent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.82}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 16.0}]}